---
title: "Embeddings and reranking"
description: "Resolve QQL vector roles, embed text and images, and choose late-interaction or cross-encoder reranking."
sidebar:
  order: 2
---

Vector names answer “which vector?” Vector roles answer “what input shape and
embedding path?” QQL keeps those decisions separate.

| Form | Role |
|---|---|
| `USING semantic` | Resolve role from collection schema |
| `USING semantic AS DENSE` | Explicit dense vector |
| `USING lexical AS SPARSE` | Explicit sparse vector |
| `USING colbert AS MULTI` | Explicit dense multivector |

{% qqlExample title="Offline-explicit vector role" %}
QUERY TEXT 'late interaction' FROM papers
USING colbert AS MULTI
LIMIT 10;
{% /qqlExample %}

## Late-interaction reranking

{% qqlExample title="ColBERT-style rerank" %}
WITH candidates AS (
  QUERY TEXT 'vector compression' USING dense LIMIT 100
)
QUERY RERANK TEXT 'vector compression' MODEL 'colbert-v2'
FROM papers
USING colbert AS MULTI
PREFETCH (candidates)
LIMIT 10;
{% /qqlExample %}

This embeds the query as a dense multivector and uses Qdrant MaxSim against the
stored multivector target.

## Cross-encoder reranking

{% qqlExample title="Host pair scoring" %}
WITH candidates AS (
  QUERY TEXT 'vector compression' USING dense LIMIT 50
)
QUERY CROSS RERANK TEXT 'vector compression'
MODEL 'bge-reranker-base'
ON FIELD abstract
FROM papers
PREFETCH (candidates)
LIMIT 10;
{% /qqlExample %}

Cross reranking reads candidate text from the payload, calls the host's
pair-scoring capability, and reorders hits client-side. It does not use a Qdrant
multivector target.
